    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d253">

                <pb facs="0488" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg388"/>

                <head>No. 253.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay
                        to Mr. Outrey.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-08-14"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 14,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 20th of June
                    last, communicating the invitation of the minister of war of France to this
                    Government to designate officers of its Army to witness certain maneuvers, on a
                    large scale, of the French troops which are to take place this autumn, and
                    referring also to the reply of the 30th of June last of this Department to your
                    note, I now have the honor to inform you that the Secretary of War, in pursuance
                    of the kind invitation of your government, has detailed Maj. A. P. Morrow, of
                    the Ninth Cavalry, First Lieut. William H. Bixby, of the Engineer Corps, and
                    First Lieut. Rogers Birnie, jr., of the Ordnance Department, to witness the
                    maneuvers in question.</p>
                <pb facs="0489" n="389" xml:id="pg389"/>
                <p>I beg you to do me the favor of conveying this information to your government,
                    and of thanking it, on behalf of the Secretary of War, for its courteous
                    invitation.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN HAY,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
